    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0350" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6354/3–2047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Bolivia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-25T16:00:00-05:00">March 25, 1947—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1320. For Bugbee<anchor n="17" xml:id="d283-f1"/> from Karl Anderson.<anchor
                        n="18" xml:id="d283-f2"/>
                    Embtel 1748, 20th.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d283-f3"/>
                    RFC made offer March 21, purchase 15,000 tons
                        Bol tin to end this year at 76 cents.</p>
                <p>Three weeks ago RFC offered price 74 cents. Since
                    then Bol-Arg
                    trade agreement signed whereby latter agrees purchase for 5 years minimum, 8,000
                    tons Bol tin annually and additional 12,000 tons
                    annually if free from other contracts at price 76 cents for 1947.</p>
                <p>After receipt latest RFC offer 76 cents Bol states impossible sell US more than 11 or
                    12,000 tons since cannot reduce Arg commitment
                    below 8,000 tons. [Anderson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
